## Why This Is Asked
Tests a practical, auditable CAPA design for IaC drift and nonconforming changes in a multi-tenant setup, plus concrete API, lifecycle, and metrics.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model
- Lifecycle state machine
- Evidence capture and auditability
- IaC drift detection and canary remediation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal API sketch for POST /caps
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => {
  // store CAPA with req.body evidence
  res.status(201).send({ id: 'CAPA-123', ...req.body });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt for audit logging and compliance needs?
- How would you prioritize CAPAs with conflicting remediation actions?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a CAPA program for data privacy incidents in a multi-tenant, real-time pipeline, balancing compliance and engineering practicality.

## Key Concepts
- Data lineage and PII tagging across streaming pipelines
- Region-aware metrics and containment strategies
- Minimal REST API design for CAPA lifecycle
- RCA templates plus staged preventive actions (canaries)
- Versioned redaction policy rollbacks and automated checks

